WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.250
Episode 2

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.250
Fire the Signal Gun!!
Space Battleship Yamato Takes Off

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.250
( Air date: Oct 13, 1974 )

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.400
Saraba Chikyuu yo

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.200
Tabidatsu fune wa...

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.000
...uchuu senkan...

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.350
...Yamato

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:40.110
Space Battleship

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:40.110
<i>YAMATO</i>

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:48.210
Ucyuu no kanata Iscandar
he unmei seoi ima tobitatsu

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.600
Kanarazu koko he kaette kuru to

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:03.400
Te wo furu hito ni egao de kotae

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:10.200
Ginga wo hanare Iscandar
he harubaru nozomu

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:16.900
Uchuu senkan Yamato

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:49.680
In 2199, Earth was
reaching its final moments.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.330
A mysterious space fleet...

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:55.570
...which began conquering known space,
had finally laid its evil hands on Earth.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:00.540
Humanity built underground cities,
and resisted them desperately...

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.430
...but they slowly lost their
ability to fight back.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.340
{IMAYA}And now Earth is falling
prey to the meteor bombs.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:21.700
Suddenly, help was offered by Iscandar
to save humanity from the contamination.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:35.830
However, Iscandar is 148,000 light
years outside the Galactic System.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:41.030
They told us that we must come
to pick up the Cosmo Cleaner-D.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:49.350
Is there a spaceship on Earth which can
withstand a journey of 148,000 light years ?

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.490
Yes, there's the Yamato.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:58.030
But the Yamato has not been
awakened from its 260 year slumber.

00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:03.430
And the radioactive poison
continues contaminating Earth.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.790
Humanity will become
extinct in only one year.

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:11.870
Unable to contact New York.
Seems to be out of energy. {sounds familiar ^_^}

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:14.900
Paris is silent.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.540
Kenya is
in a panic.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:20.940
Moscow is saying goodbye.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.440
Signals from Beijing and Rio de Janeiro have
weakened and we're unable to receive them.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.010
The radioactive contamination of the
Kanto area has advanced by 0.5 km.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.340
How is the progress
on the Yamato ?

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.430
It's behind by 3%,
but it's progressing.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.680
Commander, I'll go.
I can't wait any longer.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.830
Minor work can be
done on the voyage.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:46.920
But Okita, your health isn't...

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:51.750
The journey of 148,000 light
years may take my life...

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:56.160
...but I believe the journey to
Iscandar is worth that risk.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.720
I heard that your
scout plane crashed.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.820
I'm glad you are safe.  We can't
lose young men at a time like this.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:19.960
No, you stupid pervert.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.280
From Command HQ to cadets
Kodai Susumu and Shima Daisuke.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.790
Proceed to the waiting
air-car immediately.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:30.690
What's the matter ?

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.900
A direct call from Earth HQ.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.220
Hey, there it is.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.230
You can't come.
You're too big.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.150
I don't take
up much space.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:56.390
No, you've got nothing
to do with this.

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:59.060
You'll be punished for
ignoring your hospital work.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:02.780
I can't show my
abilities in a hospital.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.030
I don't care if you
get disassembled.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:18.390
Kodai.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.300
What is it ?

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:23.530
What, Doctor Sado ?

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.890
Hey, guys.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:30.230
Did they call you, too ?

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.080
Yep.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.250
Doctor Sado, do you
know what's going on ?

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.030
I wouldn't know.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:01.970
Where are we ?

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.430
It's a big
industrial complex.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.350
Are we going
to work here ?

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.100
What's that ?

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:21.360
What is it ?
It's huge.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.680
It looks like the
stern of a spaceship.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:36.970
Kodai, Shima, Dr. Sado,
please take elevator No. 10.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.150
It's tilted a little.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.890
Yes, it's tilted indeed.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.100
So you came.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.280
Hey, could this be...

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:17.330
Awesome.
It's a spaceship bridge.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:22.510
Kodai, Shima, welcome.  The ship is
tilted to starboard, so be careful.

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:26.090
Wha...?

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.710
What are you ?

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:38.260
I'm their best friend.

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:40.790
I request permission
to be onboard this ship.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:42.150
Granted.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:43.710
Thank you very much.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:53.480
The reason for your special mission was
to prepare you for your posts on this ship.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:58.160
You're under my command
as of now.  Work hard.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:01.440
But Captain, is
this ship complete ?

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:04.840
Unfortunately, the checkup on
the engine hasn't been finished.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:08.420
Once it's done, we can
fly with the sub-engines.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:14.890
The main engine is based on the blueprints in
the message capsule you brought from Mars.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:20.040
So it's a completely different
engine from those on Earth.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:25.000
It's called the Wave Motion engine, and
it's for the journey to planet Iscandar.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.030
Wave Motion engine ?

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:31.050
Do you mean we can fight equally
against Gamilus spaceships ?

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.110
Probably so.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:36.350
But Kodai, real combat is different
from training.  Don't take it so lightly.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:44.900
In addition, our mission has a greater
purpose above and beyond fighting Gamilus.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.240
Besides...

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:51.770
What's that ?

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:54.680
Emergency message from Earth HQ.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.180
Many fighters are
approaching this ship.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:00.100
A Gamilus spacecraft carrier
is in Earth orbit.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:04.700
Those bastards are going
to attack this ship again.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:09.300
It's directly above us,
launching fighters rapidly.

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:09.930
Bearing 202 to 304.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.520
Captain, can't this
ship fight back yet ?

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:40.720
Wait until the time comes.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:47.820
Energy charge to sub-engines is 99%.
Check the starter circuit.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:50.010
The circuit is dead,
and the sub-engines won't start.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.840
Without the sub-engines,
we're just a sitting duck.

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.900
At this rate, it's gonna be turned
into scrap without doing anything.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:13.730
Captain !

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.880
Don't panic !

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:41.550
Message from Gamilus Command
Center to the spacecraft carrier.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.180
Don't just let the fighters attack,
descend and investigate.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.330
Any hostiles
should be eliminated.

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:58.750
The circuit to the main
bridge screen is operational.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:11:59.950
Alright. Switch on.

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:10.080
Gamilus spacecraft carrier has
left lunar orbit, and is descending.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:18.330
Captain, at this rate, this
ship's going to be destroyed.

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:19.560
Can't we move yet ?

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:23.690
Final check for the sub-engines
is complete. Energy charge is 100%.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:26.030
Circuit nominal.
Starter cylinder is ready.

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:32.840
All hands,
take your positions.

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:35.580
Activate the sub-engines in 5 seconds...

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:37.030
Prepare for gun
and torpedo attack !

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.930
Connect to main power !
Turn main energy on !

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:51.370
Correct inclination !

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.490
Raise the hull !

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:53.280
Raise the hull !

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:57.010
Sub-engines, all ahead flank !
Port full !

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:00.740
It's moving.

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.340
Kodai, lead the combat crews !

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:11.830
Shima, take the pilot's seat !

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:13.890
This ship only
has engineers !

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.030
Yes, sir !

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:15.030
Yes, sir !

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:23.960
Is that...?

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:56.940
Output 120%.
Connecting power.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:00.110
Shock cannon
targeting board activated.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:01.990
Synchronizer is ready.

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:03.720
Missile launchers are ready.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:05.630
Only the Wave Motion gun on
the bow lacks sufficient power.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:09.830
Target is the space carrier.  Fire
the main guns in full automatic mode.

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:14.450
Distance 120,000.  Angle 45 degrees.
Descent velocity 1000 km/sec.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:19.260
Each gun is synched.  Automatic bearing
from 9 o'clock to 9:05, 20:45 set.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:21.150
Captain, you have control.

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:28.930
The third turret is slow by 0.2 sec. Get a grip.
Calm down, and do it just like in training.

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:32.970
Even if he says so, this is the first
time I've operated something like this.

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:50.130
All hands,
prepare for the shock.

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:52.880
Fire !

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:07.490
Gamilus Command Center.

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:10.280
The Earth base near Bogasaki was
not an ordinary underground city...

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.680
...but it was...it was a
battleship manufacturing dock.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.410
Just destroy it.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.540
My lord, unfortunately
it's too late.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.770
This ship...
this ship is already...

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:26.880
We did it.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.130
You did well.

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:41.790
Thank you.

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.030
Keep it up.

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:45.020
You too.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:49.710
Kodai, Shima.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.080
Sir.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:53.300
How is this Yamato ?

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:58.130
Space battleship Yamato.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:00.420
Is this...
that rusted scrap metal...?

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:07.400
This is the Yamato we've been
waiting for for so long.

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:38.130
According to the advanced assault unit,
a large spaceship has appeared on Earth...

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:39.680
...and our mobile
unit was destroyed.

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:45.130
The wreck we've been investigating has
been resurrected as a large class spaceship.

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:49.240
The Earthlings call it
the space battleship Yamato.

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:52.070
Lord Desler

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.750
The Yamato, you said ?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.660
Those Earthlings...

00:17:57.660 --> 00:18:01.510
Gather the space fleet, and prepare
for the Yamato's resistance operation.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:15.050
The tragedy of the Yamato started
when it was built as a battleship.

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:19.760
It's a tragedy of a ship
which was born to fight.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:31.960
Father, I hear the
sound of an engine.

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:42.920
In 1945,
WWII was about to end.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:44.830
It's the Yamato.

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.220
Yamato ?

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:50.850
Yes, look carefully.
That's the battleship Yamato.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.790
It's the ship
of Japanese men.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.110
Look carefully,
so that you don't forget.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:58.660
In 1945...

00:18:58.660 --> 00:19:02.680
...as the last fleet of the Japanese Navy,
the battleship Yamato left port...

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:09.660
...leading ten escorts to counterattack
a US fleet of more than 300 ships.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:15.250
{MOHAYA}Without escort planes and loaded with
only enough fuel for a one way trip...

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:18.930
{MOHAYA}...it was on a
suicide mission.

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:24.740
{TOKI}At 7:04am, April 6th...

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:28.680
{SENKAN}...the battleship Yamato was
attacked by about 1000 planes...

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:31.300
{SENKAN}...launched from
US aircraft carriers.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.680
We've detected
enemy aircraft.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:40.150
Bearing right 30 degrees.
Distance 200. Altitude 6000.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.580
All turrets,
target the airplanes.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.600
The clouds are low.
Watch for any sudden attack.

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.580
All hands,
abandon ship.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:33.160
Captain.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:34.180
I'll stay.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:36.150
Then I'll stay, too.

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:38.900
You idiot.  Young men
should dive and swim.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:46.280
At 3 pm, the
world's largest ship...

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:49.980
...left a huge black smoke
cloud and sank...

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:53.680
...90 miles away, 260 degrees
southeast of Bougasaki of Kyushu.

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:25.100
It might be a sad fate of a
battleship, which was built in war.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:30.710
The battleship Yamato was put to sleep
along with three thousand crewmen.

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:48.790
This space battleship Yamato
was not built to fight.

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:52.680
Originally, it was built to escape Earth
with selected people and animals...

00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:57.080
...before we were annihilated
by the radioactive poison.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:02.020
Kodai, Shima, you have trained for
a special mission to escape Earth.

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:04.130
The Yamato's
mission has changed...

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:07.510
...but you should be able to use the
skills you developed from your training.

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:08.970
I'm counting on you.

00:22:10.810 --> 00:22:14.060
I know. I'll do it for the sake of
my brother who couldn't return.

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:14.900
Please watch me.

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:24.280
148,000 light years is an almost hopelessly long journey that mankind has never attempted.

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:28.660
However, if the Wave Motion engine works,
we should be able to make it.

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:32.090
No, I'll do it,
and I'll come home.

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:10.680
Space battleship Yamato...

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:15.280
...your journey of 148,000 light years,
carrying the fate of mankind, will soon begin.

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:18.930
But the radioactive contamination
continues to progress daily.

00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:22.740
There are 364 days till
the extinction of the human race.

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:26.490
Go, Yamato, carrying the
fate of mankind on your back.

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:45.000
364 days left

00:23:47.380 --> 00:23:53.100
Okita Juzo:

00:23:47.380 --> 00:23:53.100
Naya Goro

00:23:52.640 --> 00:24:01.240
Anoko ga futteita makka na scarf

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:59.140
Starsha:

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:59.140
Hirai Michiko

00:24:00.280 --> 00:24:09.790
Note:
Originally, Oct. 13, 1974 was scheduled for the last game of Nagashima (Giants star baseball player) in Kourakuen stadium, but due to rain, Yamato ep. 2 was aired, and his final game was put off till the 14th.

00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:10.040
Dareno tame da to omotte iruka

00:24:09.790 --> 00:24:19.790
Note:
The staff was concerned about the accusation from the right wing extremists about war idealization.

00:24:09.790 --> 00:24:19.790
They realized that the imperial navy march was used in Yamato's sortie scene, so they replaced the music and made another print by noon and delivered it to Ohsaka Yomiuri TV by the Shinkansen train the day of the show.

00:24:10.040 --> 00:24:18.340
Dare no tame demo ii ja nai ka

00:24:18.340 --> 00:24:27.240
Minna sono ki de ireba ii

00:24:19.790 --> 00:24:25.790
Note:
In the ending credits, Yoko Asagami's name was misspelled as Asashimo.

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:32.920
Translation

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:32.920
Editing

00:24:27.240 --> 00:24:35.640
Tabidattsu otoko no mune ni wa

00:24:32.920 --> 00:24:40.490
Timing

00:24:32.920 --> 00:24:40.490
Song Translations

00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:43.240
Roman no kakera ga hoshii no sa

00:24:40.490 --> 00:24:48.490
A

00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:47.240
La la la...

00:24:47.240 --> 00:24:51.240
La la la...

00:24:51.240 --> 00:25:01.140
La la la, makka na scarf
